WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.732
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Morning Bridge.

00:00:13.732 --> 00:00:19.464
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:19.464 --> 00:00:22.903
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:22.903 --> 00:00:26.343
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:26.343 --> 00:00:34.368
Every morning, you make a crossing. You leave the feeling of home, and you arrive at the feeling of school.

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:43.539
Home feeling and school feeling are both real. Neither one is the problem. The crossing itself is the thing.

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:53.857
A bridge helps you cross. This bridge has three parts, and you already carry all three.

00:00:53.857 --> 00:00:58.442
Let me show you the bridge you walk every morning.

00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:08.760
Part one: name one thing you carry from home. A hug. A song. The smell of breakfast. It travels with you — nothing says you have to leave it behind.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:19.078
Part two: name one thing waiting for you at school. A friend's face. Your chair. A book you like. Something on this side is glad you came.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:29.396
Part three: one slow breath, right in the middle. That breath is the bridge itself. You are not at home. You are not all the way at school. You are crossing.

00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:38.567
Carry one thing. Name one thing. Breathe one breath. That is the whole bridge.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:39.714
And the bridge works both ways. At the end of the day, you cross back — carrying school things home.

00:01:39.714 --> 00:01:50.031
Some mornings the crossing is easy. Some mornings it is not. A hard morning is allowed to be hard.

00:01:50.031 --> 00:02:00.349
If you are missing someone, that missing is not a problem to fix. Missing someone means they matter. It can ride along with you all day, quietly.

00:02:00.349 --> 00:02:08.374
Nobody here will ask you for details. Your morning is yours. The bridge does not need the story — only the crossing.

00:02:08.374 --> 00:02:09.520
However this morning felt, you are here now. And here has things waiting for you.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:17.545
One thing I carry. One thing waiting. One slow breath.

00:02:17.545 --> 00:02:23.277
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:23.277 --> 00:02:27.863
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:27.863 --> 00:02:33.595
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:33.595 --> 00:02:39.327
You're ready for what's next.
